        synopsis {commit_hw_sysmon ?-quiet? ?-verbose? hw_objects}
        description {Writes the current property values of a hw_sysmon object to the system monitor registers of the hardware device. Changes to properties such as the CONFIG_REG properties are not written to the device until this command is run. The monitor may be given as the hw_sysmon object itself or reached through the associated hw_device, hw_target, or hw_server object, and at least one object is required.}
        returns {Nothing.}
        example {set_property CONFIG_REG.BU 1 [get_hw_sysmon]
commit_hw_sysmon [lindex [get_hw_sysmons] 0]}
        source {Xilinx UG835 2026.1}
    }
}
