        summary {Get or set the current hardware ILA.}
        synopsis {current_hw_ila ?-quiet? ?-verbose? ?hw_ila?}
        description {Sets or returns the current hardware Integrated Logic Analyzer debug core targeted by the Hardware Manager for programming and debug. ILA cores let you probe specific signals, trigger on programmed hardware events, and capture data from the device in real time; they are added by instantiating an ILA core from the IP catalog or with create_debug_core. After programming the device, the cores in the design are accessible with get_hw_ilas and their probes with get_hw_probes.}
        returns {Hardware ILA.}
        example {current_hw_ila}
        source {Xilinx UG835 2026.1}
    }
}
command current_hw_ila_data {
