        synopsis {current_hw_ila_data ?-quiet? ?-verbose? ?hw_ila_data?}
        description {Sets or returns the current ILA debug core data object, which is created by upload_hw_ila_data or read_hw_ila_data and by default is the latest one created by the Vivado logic analyzer. The ILA core captures sample data in real time as the device runs, based on the event triggers or capture conditions defined on the hw_ila object and armed by run_hw_ila. The data object can be shown with display_hw_ila_data or written to disk with write_hw_ila_data.}
        returns {Hardware ILA data.}
        example {current_hw_ila_data}
        source {Xilinx UG835 2026.1}
