        summary {Delete one or more user defined DRC rule deck objects.}
        synopsis {delete_drc_ruledeck ?-regexp? ?-nocase? ?-filter expression? ?-quiet? ?-verbose? ?patterns?}
        description {Deletes user-defined drc_ruledeck objects matching the given patterns from the current project; the default pattern is the wildcard '*', which deletes all user-defined rule decks. A rule deck is a collection of design rule checks grouped for convenience to be run with report_drc at different stages of the flow, created by create_drc_ruledeck. Factory defined rule decks cannot be deleted, the deck need not be empty, and a deleted deck cannot be restored by undo.}
        returns {Drc_ruledeck.}
        example {delete_drc_ruledeck}
        source {Xilinx UG835 2026.1}
