        description {Gets the configuration flash memory devices supported by the Vivado Design Suite or Vivado Lab Edition, matched against the search patterns, which default to the wildcard *. An FPGA can be configured from such an external nonvolatile memory device; create_hw_cfgmem defines a flash memory device used for configuring and booting the hardware device, and the Vivado Lab Edition supports hw_device objects only, not part objects. This command returns a list of cfgmem_part objects that match the specified search criteria, or returns an error if it fails.}
        returns {List of cfgmem_part objects.}
