        summary {Get a list of hardware ILA debug cores.}
        synopsis {get_hw_ilas ?-of_objects hw_devices? ?-regexp? ?-nocase? ?-filter expression? ?-quiet? ?-verbose? ?patterns?}
        description {Returns the Integrated Logic Analyzer (ILA) debug core objects defined on the current hardware device, which let you probe specific signals, trigger on programmed hardware events, and capture data from the device in real time. ILA cores are added into the RTL sources or into the synthesized netlist with create_debug_core, written to a probes file with write_debug_probes, and programmed onto the device with program_hw_devices together with the bitstream; the design debug cores returned by get_debug_cores are related to but separate from these hardware debug cores. This command returns a list of ILA debug core objects on the device, or returns an error if it fails.}
        returns {Hardware ILAs.}
        example {get_hw_ilas -of_objects [current_hw_device]}
        source {Xilinx UG835 2026.1}
