        description {Returns the hw_mig objects on the current hardware device, one per debug-enabled memory controller implemented into the design. Memory IP from the IP catalog generates memory controllers and interfaces, implemented during opt_design or manually with implement_mig_cores; the hw_mig object carries the properties needed to get the calibration status and draw the per-bit eye margin views, letting you verify calibration and read window margins in the memory interface design. This command returns a list of hw_mig objects on the current hardware device, or returns an error if it fails.}
        returns {Hardware migs cores.}
        example {get_hw_migs -of_objects [current_hw_target]}
