        summary {Get a list of hardware probes.}
        synopsis {get_hw_probes ?-of_objects objects? ?-regexp? ?-nocase? ?-filter expression? ?-quiet? ?-verbose? ?patterns?}
        description {Returns the hw_probe objects in the Hardware Manager that are defined on signals in the design, or that are assigned to the specified ILA or VIO debug cores. Probes can be added to ILA cores in the synthesized netlist with create_debug_port and connected to design signals with connect_debug_port, while VIO probes can only be added when the IP core is customized from the IP catalog; probes are written to a probes file with write_debug_probes and programmed onto the device with program_hw_devices. This command returns a list of debug probe objects on the device, or returns an error if it fails.}
        returns {Hardware probes.}
        example {get_hw_probes -of_object [current_hw_ila]}
        source {Xilinx UG835 2026.1}
