        synopsis {get_hw_sio_iberts ?-of_objects objects? ?-regexp? ?-nocase? ?-filter expression? ?-quiet? ?-verbose? ?patterns?}
        description {Returns the Integrated Bit Error Ratio Tester (IBERT) debug core objects, hw_sio_ibert, defined on the current hardware device. The IBERT core enables in-system serial I/O validation and debug and lets you configure and control the major features of the GTs on the device, including TX pre-emphasis and post-emphasis, TX differential swing, RX equalization, the Decision Feedback Equalizer, and PLL divider settings. This command returns a list of IBERT debug core objects on the device, or returns an error if it fails.}
        returns {Hardware SIO IBERT cores.}
        example {get_hw_sio_iberts -of_objects [current_hw_device]}
        source {Xilinx UG835 2026.1}
    }
}
