        summary {Get a list of hardware SIO PLLs.}
        synopsis {get_hw_sio_plls ?-of_objects objects? ?-regexp? ?-nocase? ?-filter expression? ?-quiet? ?-verbose? ?patterns?}
        description {Returns the PLL objects, hw_sio_pll, defined on the IBERT debug core on the current hardware device. Each serial transceiver channel has a ring Channel PLL (CPLL), and in UltraScale and 7 series FPGAs the GTX adds a shared Quad PLL (QPLL) per quad; on the device the GTXE2_CHANNEL component holds the transceiver and CPLL units while GTXE2_COMMON holds the QPLL unit. This command returns a list of all PLL objects, both CPLLs and QPLLs, on the device, or returns an error if it fails.}
        returns {Hardware SIO PLLs.}
        example {join [get_hw_sio_plls -of [get_hw_sio_iberts] ] \n}
        source {Xilinx UG835 2026.1}
    }
}
