        synopsis {get_hw_sio_sweeps ?-of_objects objects? ?-regexp? ?-nocase? ?-filter expression? ?-quiet? ?-verbose? ?patterns?}
        description {Returns the serial I/O analyzer link sweep objects defined on the IBERT debug core, which are collections of link scans run across a range of GT configuration settings to help determine which settings are best for the design. A returned sweep object can be used with run_hw_sio_sweep to run analysis on the specified links or GT receivers, saved to disk with write_hw_sio_sweep, and removed with remove_hw_sio_sweep. This command returns one or more hw_sio_sweep objects, or returns an error if the command fails.}
        returns {Hardware SIO sweeps.}
        example {get_hw_sio_sweeps}
        source {Xilinx UG835 2026.1}
    }
}
