        synopsis {get_hw_sio_txs ?-of_objects objects? ?-regexp? ?-nocase? ?-filter expression? ?-quiet? ?-verbose? ?patterns?}
        description {Returns the transmitter objects, hw_sio_tx, of the Gigabit Transceivers that are in use on the IBERT debug core on the current hardware device. Each GT includes an independent transmitter consisting of a PCS and a PMA, through which parallel data flows from the device logic into the TX interface, through the PCS and PMA, and out the TX driver as high-speed serial data. This command returns a list of transmitter objects on the device, or returns an error if it fails.}
        returns {Hardware SIO TXs.}
        example {join [get_hw_sio_txs] \n}
