        synopsis {get_hw_vios ?-of_objects hw_devices? ?-regexp? ?-nocase? ?-filter expression? ?-quiet? ?-verbose? ?patterns?}
        description {Returns the Virtual Input/Output (VIO) debug core objects defined on the current hardware device. The VIO core can both monitor and drive internal signals on a programmed FPGA in real time, using hw_probe objects as input probes that monitor signals and output probes that drive them, with values driven onto the signals by commit_hw_vio. The VIO core must be instantiated in the RTL code from the IP catalog. This command returns a list of VIO debug core objects on the device, or returns an error if it fails.}
        returns {Hardware VIOs.}
        example {get_hw_vios -of_objects [current_hw_device]}
        source {Xilinx UG835 2026.1}
    }
}
