        summary {Recompile the design and restart the current simulation.}
        synopsis {relaunch_sim ?-quiet? ?-verbose?}
        description {Suspends the current simulation, recompiles the current design into a new simulation snapshot without changing the compilation options, then connects the current simulation to the new snapshot and restarts it. The current simulator configuration, such as open waveform and code windows and the Scopes and Objects window settings, is preserved; the command applies only to simulations running in the Vivado IDE, not to stand-alone or batch simulator runs.}
        returns {Current simulation object.}
        example {relaunch_sim}
        source {Xilinx UG835 2026.1}
    }
}
